  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic local HTTP fixture measures frontend mechanics, not production database/network latency.",
    "Clean cells retain light RAF/long-task/CDP observation overhead; instrumented cells separately attribute compiled production bindings.",
    "Bridge entry is synchronous callback invocation elapsed; lifetime includes awaits and is not CPU. Nested parse/update/draw and CDP style/layout can overlap; never sum these into exclusive CPU or wall time.",
    "Raw parse units are UTF-16 code units. Worker durations use worker-local clocks.",
    "DOM bounds are sampled at phase boundaries, not a full heap or every transient frame measurement.",
    "Task dock supports active readers only. Sealed task-linked reader uses canonical task-filtered full Sessions route; Evidence-click navigation is not measured.",
    "Finite workflow deadlines are correctness/cleanup guards, not latency budgets. No cross-machine, cross-browser, or hard timing threshold is introduced."
  ]
